":"like the bird"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"அளி","parts":[{"text":"அளி","lemma":"aḷi","gloss":"grace"}],"gloss":"grace"},{"surface":"நசைக்கு","parts":[{"text":"நசை","lemma":"nacai","gloss":"desire"},{"text":"கு","lemma":"ku","gloss":"for"}],"gloss":"for the desire"},{"surface":"இரங்கி","parts":[{"text":"இரங்கு","lemma":"iraṅku","gloss":"yearn"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"yearning"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அடி","parts":[{"text":"அடி","lemma":"aṭi","gloss":"feet"}],"gloss":"feet"},{"surface":"நிழல்","parts":[{"text":"நிழல்","lemma":"niḻal","gloss":"shade"}],"gloss":"shade"},{"surface":"பழகிய","parts":[{"text":"பழகு","lemma":"paḻaku","gloss":"accustom"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"iya","gloss":"adjectival suffix"}],"gloss":"accustomed"},{"surface":"அடியுறை","parts":[{"text":"அடி","lemma":"aṭi","gloss":"feet"},{"text":"உறை","lemma":"uṟai","gloss":"dwelling/servant"}],"gloss":"servant dwelling at the feet"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கடு","parts":[{"text":"கடு","lemma":"kaṭu","gloss":"swift"}],"gloss":"swift"},{"surface":"மான்","parts":[{"text":"மான்","lemma":"māṉ","gloss":"horse"}],"gloss":"horse"},{"surface":"மாற","parts":[{"text":"மாற","lemma":"மாற","gloss":"O Maṟaṉ!"}],"gloss":"O Maṟaṉ!","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மறவாதீமே","parts":[{"text":"மறவாது","lemma":"maṟavātu","gloss":"without forgetting"},{"text":"ஈமே","lemma":"īmē","gloss":"do/give (imperative suffix)"}],"gloss":"do not forget!"}]}],"literal":"Like a great mountain where a waterfall descends / with a sandalwood garland shining on his chest, unceasing / divine, filled with chastity, beautifully jeweled woman / gentle woman given birth to, sapphire-resembling beautiful mouth / tinkling anklet sons may flourish, saying and praising / strong chariot lord, you praising / affection because of not obtaining, even in dreams crying out my / desirable heart being delighted to rejoice / banyan tree residing god like your wealth / spear having lord I saw, therefore / I have sent, may you live long, your garland strung / cool Tamil territory inside as plunder / bowing down, gathering, consuming, gem-like, great, fierce strength / those like you, like your sons, always / enemies to wither, precious ornaments giving, your / gold-possessing great palace to fill, who kept your / ancestors may they be like, their great benevolence / always, every day increasing, gathering waves / great ocean more than the water, that ocean's more than the sand / stretching high of the sky more than the raindrops, exceedingly / they begetting sons every time you see, you too / desired with wealth, fame pleasantly shining / long may you live, great noble one, and I / kin without distant from the country, every day / raindrop desiring like the bird, your grace for the desire yearning, your / feet shade accustomed servant dwelling at the feet / swift horse O Maṟaṉ, do not forget!","translation":"Like a great mountain down which a waterfall cascades, your chest is adorned with a fragrant sandalwood garland. I praised you, the lord of strong chariots, wishing that the young sons with sapphire-like mouths and tinkling anklets, born to your gentle queen of divine chastity, may flourish. My longing heart, which used to cry out even in dreams because it had not received your affection, now rejoices in delight. O spear-bearing lord, I have beheld your wealth, which is like that of the great God who sits beneath the banyan tree. Therefore, I have sent my prayers; may you live long! May your sons, who possess gem-like, fierce strength and who make the cool Tamil land their plunder, bringing tribute from those who bow to them, be like your ancestors who filled your golden palace with precious ornaments won from withered enemies. May their great benevolence increase day by day, more numerous than the waters of the wave-tossed ocean, more than the sands of that shore, and more than the raindrops from the high sky. Every time you behold the sons they beget, may you too shine with desired wealth and fame, and live a long life, O noble lord! As for me, even when I am in a distant land without kin, I yearn for your grace like a cātaka bird that longs for raindrops. O Maṟaṉ of swift horses, do not forget me, your servant accustomed to the shade of your feet!","modern":"அருவி வீழும் பெரிய மலையைப் போல, சந்தனக் கலவையுடன் விளங்கும் மார்பினையும், நீங்காத தெய்வத் தன்மை பொருந்திய கற்பினையும், சிறந்த அணிகலன்களையும் உடைய உன் மனைவி பெற்றெடுத்த, நீலமணி போன்ற அழகிய வாயினையும் சிலம்பினையும் உடைய புதல்வர்கள் சிறந்து விளங்குவார்களாக என்று வாழ்த்தி, வலிய தேரையுடைய தலைவனே, உன்னைப் பாராட்டி, உன் அன்பைப் பெறாததால் கனவிலும் கதறும் எனது விருப்பம் மிக்க நெஞ்சம் மகிழ்ந்து உவகை கொள்ளுமாறு, ஆலமரத்தின் கீழ் அமர்ந்திருக்கும் சிவபெருமானைப் போன்ற உனது செல்வத்தை, வேல் ஏந்திய தலைவனே, நான் கண்டேன். ஆதலால், உன்னை வாழ்த்தி விடைபெறுகிறேன். உனது மாலை சூடிய குளிர்ந்த தமிழ்நாட்டின் எல்லையைக் கைப்பற்றி, உனக்குக் கீழ்ப்படிந்து திறை செலுத்தி உண்ணும், நீலமணி போன்ற பெரிய வலிமையும் மிக்க திறமையும் உடைய உன்னைப் போன்ற உனது புதல்வர்கள், எப்போதும் பகைவர்கள் அழியுமாறு அரிய அணிகலன்களைக் கொண்டுவந்து உனது பொன்னாலான பெரிய அரண்மனை நிறைய வைத்த உனது முன்னோர்களைப் போல விளங்குவார்களாக! இவர்களது பெரிய இரக்கக் குணம் எப்போதும் பெருகி, அலைகள் நிறைந்த பெரிய கடலின் நீரைக் காட்டிலும், அக்கடலின் மணலைக் காட்டிலும், உயர்ந்த வானத்தின் மழைத்துளிகளைக் காட்டிலும் மிகுதியாக விளங்குவதாக! இவர்கள் பெறும் புதல்வர்களைக் காணும்போதெல்லாம் நீயும் விரும்பிய செல்வத்தோடு புகழ் பெற்று இனிது விளங்கி நெடுங்காலம் வாழ்வாயாக! பெருந்தகையே, உறவினர்கள் இல்லாத தொலைதூர நாட்டில் இருந்தாலும், மழைத்துளியை விரும்பும் வானம்பாடிப் பறவையைப் போல உனது அருளை விரும்பி ஏங்கி, உனது திருவடி நிழலில் பழகிய உனது அடியவனாகிய என்னை, விரைந்து செல்லும் குதிரைகளையுடைய மாறனே, என்றும் மறவாமல் இருப்பாயாக!","explanation":"The poet Vaṭamavaṇṇakkaṉ Pēricāttaṉār addresses the Pandya king Ilavantikaip paḷḷit tuñciya Naṉmāṟaṉ in this poem of the pāṭāṇ tiṇai. The poet praises the king's family, specifically wishing long life and prosperity to his young sons and future descendants. He compares the king's chest, smeared with sandalwood paste, to a great mountain with a cascading waterfall. The poet's deep yearning for the king's patronage is beautifully illustrated through the image of the cātaka bird (puḷ), which is believed to survive only on raindrops and waits anxiously for the clouds to pour. Key words such as 'அடிநிழல்' (shade of the feet) and 'அளிநசை' (desire for grace) emphasize the poet's absolute dependence on the king's benevolence.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,1.0],[1.0,1.4],[1.4,1.7],[1.7,2.4],[2.4,2.6],[2.6,3.0],[3.0,3.6],[3.6,4.7],[4.7,5.0],[5.0,5.5],[5.5,5.6],[5.6,6.2],[6.4,7.1],[7.1,7.3],[7.3,7.88],[7.88,9.17],[9.17,9.68],[9.68,9.75],[9.9,10.2],[10.2,10.5],[10.5,11.4],[11.4,11.6],[11.6,12.0],[12.0,12.2],[12.2,13.5],[13.5,13.8],[13.8,14.2],[14.2,14.2],[14.2,16.4],[16.4,16.8],[16.8,16.9],[16.9,17.4],[18.4,19.1],[19.1,19.3],[19.3,19.9],[19.9,20.3],[20.3,20.9],[20.9,21.2],[21.2,21.8],[21.8,22.0],[22.0,22.34],[22.34,23.7],[23.7,24.0],[24.0,24.2],[24.2,24.8],[24.8,25.77],[25.77,26.5],[26.5,26.75],[26.75,26.75],[26.75,26.75],[26.75,27.3],[27.3,27.3],[27.3,27.3],[27.3,28.8],[28.8,30.8],[30.8,31.2],[31.2,31.3],[31.3,32.6],[32.6,32.8],[32.8,33.1],[33.1,33.67],[33.67,33.9],[33.9,34.8],[34.8,35.1],[35.1,35.4],[35.4,36.1],[36.88,37.48],[37.48,37.78],[37.78,37.98],[37.98,38.53],[38.53,38.88],[38.88,39.88],[39.88,39.88],[39.88,40.18],[40.42,40.98],[40.98,42.18],[42.18,42.48],[42.48,42.68],[42.68,43.28],[43.28,44.78],[44.78,45.18],[45.18,45.38],[45.38,45.68],[45.68,47.08],[47.08,47.58],[47.58,47.98],[47.98,48.28],[48.28,49.48],[49.48,49.58],[49.58,50.68],[50.68,50.98],[50.98,51.88],[51.88,52.28],[52.28,52.38],[52.38,53.08],[53.08,54.13],[54.13,54.31],[54.48,54.88],[54.88,55.05],[55.1,55.38],[56.12,56.92],[56.92,57.42],[57.42,58.32],[